With the construction and installation of the new gain monitor chamber complete, we are able to measure the TPC gas gain directly and as such may be able to improve the measurement of dE/dx and PID at STAR. A source of radiation with a known energy is used to ionize the TPC gas flowing through the chamber. The deposited charge accelerates toward the chamber's high voltage anode wires

Figure 2.10: The gain monitor chamber with the wire planes and the shielded electronics exposed. The shielding for the wire planes and the Fe\({}^{55}\) source are not shown. The aluminum outer housing is folded back and locked into place when the chamber is in use so that the high-voltage wires are not exposed.

