#### Systematic Uncertainties and Correlations Unrelated to the Reaction Plane

Sources of systematic error in the calculation of \(v_{2}\) are correlations unrelated to the reaction plane (non-flow effects), estimation of the yield from the invariant mass distributions, the \(p_{T}\) resolution (\(\delta p_{T}/p_{T}\)), and biases introduced by the cuts used in the analysis. Table 3.7 lists the dominant systematic errors for \(K_{S}^{0}\) and \(\Lambda+\overline{\Lambda}\)\(v_{2}\). The systematic error in \(v_{2}\) associated with the yield extraction is found to be small and the non-flow systematic error is dominant.

