The differential cross-section for particle production, is found by counting the number of particles \(d^{3}n\) produced in a phase space element. It's advantageous to define the phase-space element to be Lorentz invariant. The usual choice is the element \(dp_{x}dp_{y}dp_{z}/E\), so that the invariant cross-section is

